-- 22 listed places carried a website title or their other trading names as
-- their name: "Sheesh Mayfair | Best Turkish Restaurants and Nightclubs in
-- London | Cocktail Bar | Nightclub", "The Standard - Voted Best Indian on
-- Bricklane", a dark kitchen's eight brands joined with slashes. The name shows
-- on cards, the place page and Google, and from the outreach emails too.
--
-- Found 2026-11-01. Each new name only cuts words from the old one, never adds
-- any: the first trading name, without slogans, other brands or a trailing
-- space. Three were left alone because which part is the name is not clear
-- ("Par London - Pak Al Reyan Restaurant", "Chopstix - London Brent Cross",
-- "Las Iguanas - London - Stratford Westfield"). Slugs do not change, so no
-- link breaks. The weekly hygiene refresh never writes names, so they stay.
--
-- A row changes only while its name is still exactly the old one.

update public.restaurants set name = 'DONNER & SHISH' where id = 'f0453de9-2de6-426e-a7af-ef038911796e' and name = 'DONNER & SHISH, authentic Turkish kebab, grill, delicious pizza, halal';
